="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ninurta-kudurri-usur I was king of Babylon for about three years in the late 10th century BCE, the second ruler of the Bazi Dynasty after Eulmash-shakin-shumi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/nioro-du-sahel"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/nioro-du-sahel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Nioro du Sahel</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Nioro du Sahel is a town in the Kayes Region of western Mali, close to the border with Mauritania.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/nippur"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/nippur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Nippur</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Nippur was an ancient city in southern Mesopotamia, the religious centre of Sumer and home of the temple of the god Enlil.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/niqmaddu-ii"><span class="enc-name">Niqmaddu II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Niqmaddu II was a king of Ugarit on the Syrian coast in the 14th century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/niqmaddu-iii"><span class="enc-name">Niqmaddu III</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Niqmaddu III was king of Ugarit in the late thirteenth century BCE, the son and successor of Ibiranu.</span></a></li></ul>
